.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions are used to specify search criteria to help search for
specific objects through other names than just the URI that's given to
.Xr OSSL_STORE_open 3 .
For example, this can be useful for an application that has received a
URI and then wants to add on search criteria in a uniform and supported
manner.
.Ss Types
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
is an opaque type that holds the constructed search criterion, and that
can be given to an OSSL_STORE context with
.Xr OSSL_STORE_find 3 .
.Pp
The calling application owns the allocation of an
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
at all times, and should therefore be careful not to deallocate it
before
.Xr OSSL_STORE_close 3
has been called for the OSSL_STORE context it was given to.
.Ss Application Functions
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_name ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_issuer_serial ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_key_fingerprint ,
and
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_alias
are used to create an
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
from a subject name, an issuer name and serial number pair, a key
fingerprint, and an alias (for example a friendly name).
The parameters that are provided are not copied, only referred to in a
criterion, so they must have at least the same life time as the created
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_free
is used to free the
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Ss Loader Functions
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get_type
returns the criterion type for the given
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH .
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_name ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_serial ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_bytes ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_string ,
and
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_digest
are used to retrieve different data from a
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH ,
as available for each type.
For more information, see
.Sx SUPPORTED CRITERION TYPES
below.
.Sh SUPPORTED CRITERION TYPES
Currently supported criterion types are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_BY_NAME
This criterion supports a search by exact match of subject name.
The subject name itself is a
.Vt X509_NAME
pointer.
A criterion of this type is created with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_name ,
and the actual subject name is retrieved with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_name .
.It OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_BY_ISSUER_SERIAL
This criterion supports a search by exact match of both issuer name and
serial number.
The issuer name itself is a
.Vt X509_NAME
pointer, and the serial number is a
.Sy ASN1_INTEGER
pointer.
A criterion of this type is created with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_issuer_serial
and the actual issuer name and serial number are retrieved with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_name
and
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_serial .
.It OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_BY_KEY_FINGERPRINT
This criterion supports a search by exact match of key fingerprint.
The key fingerprint in itself is a string of bytes and its length, as
well as the algorithm that was used to compute the fingerprint.
The digest may be left unspecified (NULL), and in that case, the loader
has to decide on a default digest and compare fingerprints accordingly.
A criterion of this type is created with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_key_fingerprint
and the actual fingerprint and its length can be retrieved with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_bytes .
The digest can be retrieved with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_digest .
.It OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_BY_ALIAS
This criterion supports a search by match of an alias of some kind.
The alias in itself is a simple C string.
A criterion of this type is created with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_alias
and the actual alias is retrieved with
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_string .
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_name ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_issuer_serial ,
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_key_fingerprint ,
and
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_by_alias
return a
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
pointer on success, or NULL on failure.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get_type
returns the criterion type of the given
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH .
There is no error value.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_name
returns a
.Vt X509_NAME
pointer on success, or NULL when the given
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
was of a different type.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_serial
returns a
.Sy ASN1_INTEGER
pointer on success, or NULL when the given
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
was of a different type.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_bytes
returns a
.Sy const unsigned char
pointer and sets
.Em *length
to the strings length on success, or NULL when the given
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
was of a different type.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_string
returns a
.Sy const char
pointer on success, or NULL when the given
.Vt OSSL_STORE_SEARCH
was of a different type.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_STORE_SEARCH_get0_digest
returns a
.Sy const EVP_MD
pointer.
NULL is a valid value and means that the store loader default will be
used when applicable.
